# Same molecule/basis as h2.inp, but with an extreme speed of light. At this
# basis size (cc-pVTZ), diagonalizing the full H_RKB_ortho at c=1e7 still
# shows severe floating-point breakdown in the printed "Max |E(even) -
# E(odd)|" and eigenvector-partner-deviation checks: that matrix's
# Small-Small block is built as -2c^2*S + V summed in double precision, and
# by c=1e7, -2c^2 ~ -2e14 swamps V's ~O(1) contribution to well below
# double precision's ~16 significant digits. This is an intrinsic
# limitation of diagonalizing that particular (huge-magnitude) matrix with
# double-precision LAPACK, not something a different basis or a bigger
# speed of light can dodge.
#
# The separate "Positive-energy eigenvalues" section (always printed after
# it) avoids this entirely, via an exact Feshbach/Loewdin reduction that
# never forms that -2c^2+V sum: its Kramers-pair splitting stays exactly
# 0.000000 here, and at c=1e10 too -- see RkbPositiveEnergyHamiltonian.h.
# That is the branch to look at for the nonrelativistic limit / Kramers
# symmetry at extreme c; the raw H_RKB_ortho spectrum's negative-energy
# branch remains inherently ill-conditioned at this scale.
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
SPEED_OF_LIGHT = 10000000
NELEC 2
BASIS h2-cc-pvtz.gbs

GEOMETRY
H   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   0.741400
END
